{title: One Thing Remains (FJ_96_en)}
{song_number: 96}
{language: en}
{artist: Jeremy Riddle; Brian Johnson; Christa Black}
{tempo: 74}

{start_of_verse: 1}
Higher [A]than the mountains that I [E]face, stronger [A]than the power of the [E]grave.
[A]Constant in the trial and the [E]change: one [A]thing [E]re[B]mains, one [A]thing [E]re[B]mains.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
Your [C#m7]love never fails, it [A]never gives up,
it [E]never runs out on [B]me.
Your [C#m7]love never fails, it [A]never gives up,
it [E]never runs out on [B]me.
It [E]never runs out on [B]me.
Your [E]love, Your [C#m]love.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
On and [A]on and on and on it [E]goes. It o[A]verwhelms and satisfies my [E]soul.
And I [A]never ever have to be a[E]fraid.
One [A]thing [E]re[B]mains, one [A]thing [E]re[B]mains.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
Your [C#m7]love never fails, it [A]never gives up,
it [E]never runs out on [B]me.
Your [C#m7]love never fails, it [A]never gives up,
it [E]never runs out on [B]me.
